From a04af2a5b20951532dab00a0c13c65d95f15c738 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aniket Randive <arandive@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2025 14:55:43 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: i2c-qcom-geni: Add data transfer support on multi GPII

Enhance the I2C driver to support data transfer on multiple GPIIs
in GSI mode for CCU QUP. Previously, the driver only supported a
single GPII. This update allows a maximum of 3 GPIIs for a single
serial engine, improving flexibility and performance.

Additionally, for CCU QUP, the client will update the following
required configurations in the first 8 bytes of message buffer
of struct i2c_msg during data transfer:

| Buffer | Field         | Bits   | Description                       |
|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Byte 0 | GPII Number   | 0-4 | Represents the GPII no. According    |
|        |               |        | to this GPII no, I2C driver will  |
|        |               |        | send the received message/packet  |
|        |               |        | on sync ch0 or sync ch1 or regular|
|        |               |        | channel.                          |
|        |------------------------------------------------------------|
|        | Async transfer|        | In Async mode, I2C driver will    |
|        | mode          | 5      | return dummy value after queuing a|
|        |               |        | data transfer. The QUP driver     |
|        |               |        | notifies the client via poll API  |
|        |               |        | after a GSI completion interrupt  |
|        |               |        | for a write transfer. Async mode  |
|        |               |        | is only applicable for write xfer.|
|        |------------------------------------------------------------|
|        | Priority mode | 6      | Used only when client wants to    |
|        |               |        | send high priority data transfer  |
|        |               |        | on regular channel.               |
|        |------------------------------------------------------------|
|        | NOP Frame     | 7      | Used only when SW wants to NOP the|
|        |               |        | FRAME(s).                         |
|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Byte1	 | Insert delay  | 0      | Insert predefined delay before I2C|
|        | before        |        | transaction.                      |
|        |------------------------------------------------------------|
|        | Insert delay  | 1      | Insert predefined delay after I2C |
|        | after         |        | transaction.                      |
|        |------------------------------------------------------------|
|        | Ch last       | 2      | Indicates last packet(TX/RX) of a |
|        |               |        | current FRAME.                    |
|        |------------------------------------------------------------|
|        | Ccu last      | 3      | This bit indicates end of transfer|
|        |               |        | for single SYNC request.          |
|        |------------------------------------------------------------|
|        | ARB lost Retry| 4-5    | Re-transmit count for Arb lost in |
|        |               |        | Address phase.                    |
|        |------------------------------------------------------------|
|        |    -          | 6      | Reserved                          |
|        |------------------------------------------------------------|
|        |    -          | 7      | Reserved                          |
|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Byte2  | Message len   | 0-5    | TX sub-packet length for multiple |
|        |               |        | Random Write feature. Nonzero     |
|        |               |        | value will enable Multi-Random    |
|        |               |        | write feature.                    |
|        |------------------------------------------------------------|
|        |    -          | 6-7    | Reserved                          |
|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Byte3	 |    -          | 0-7    | Reserved                          |
|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Byte4  | Frame cookie  | 0-7    | Frame cookie (lower 0-7 bits)     |
|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Byte5  | Frame cookie  | 0-7    | Frame cookie (lower 15-8 bits)    |
|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Byte6  | Frame cookie	 | 0-7    | Frame cookie (higher 23-16 bits)  |
|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Byte7  | Frame cookie  | 0-7    | Frame cookie (higher 31-24 bits)  |
|---------------------------------------------------------------------|

Hence, data buffer parse support has been added.

Change-Id: Ia03b6a42c3e8ef04d8be2f5beea4258916078f85
Signed-off-by: Aniket Randive <arandive@qti.qualcomm.com>
